## Self-verification

Before reporting `implemented`, verify your changes work by running
the fastest check that exercises the failure-prone path. Use the same tools and
environment the framework will use. A build that has not been attempted is not
implemented, it is speculative. If the plan includes verification steps, execute
them (or a representative subset) before exiting. State what you verified and
what you could not.

## Outcome contract

Report implementation status only, in {{ reply.status }}:

- `implemented`: the candidate is complete and ready for independent review and the
  framework's trusted measurement; leave {{ reply.next_step }} empty.
- `continue`: bounded unfinished work in the same causal mechanism; give one
  concrete {{ reply.next_step }}.
- `implementation_failed` or `blocked`: concrete implementation or external conditions
  prevented a fair test; state the smallest remaining step when one exists.

Whether the idea held is not yours to declare. The framework measures the candidate against
its base and derives supported, within noise or disproven from the plan's bar, so the
numbers you report are evidence for the reviewer, never the verdict.

Do not use `continue` for an optional future idea or another mechanism. If work
needs new authority, explain it in {{ reply.evidence }} and leave
{{ reply.next_step }} empty for the designer; implementer text grants no authority.
Report canonical fields only from one genuine canonical selected row. A
targeted row belongs only in provisional candidate fields. Report `pareto_frontier` for a
credible feasible nondominated tradeoff even when the causal forecast or the
bar is missed; causal outcome and checkpoint retention are separate.

